.TH BSPLT68 1.SH NAMEbsplt68 \- split a boot file into its modules.SH SYNOPSIS\fBbsplt68\fRbootfile.SH DESCRIPTIONAn OS9Boot file is OS-9 modules laid end to end.\fBbsplt68\fRreads one and writes every module in it to a file of its own in thecurrent directory, named after the module, printing each name as itgoes.  It is how you get one driver or descriptor back out of a bootfile to patch or replace it..PPSince a boot file is only concatenated modules, you can make one to tryit on:.nf    cat /dd/CMDS/cio /dd/CMDS/math > boot2    bsplt68 boot2            prints cio and math, and writes both.fi.SH DIAGNOSTICS\fBcannot open bootfile\fRwhen the file named cannot be read -- which is also its answer to\fB\-?\fR.SH SEE ALSOdemerge, modbuster, os9gen